<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:57Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russian birth tourism to Brazil increases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6219b17816300a9ca6ca68126cdeb9a403e3588423fc8392c943113f23ad0b68</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T19:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304--01a0fcbb92e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine and stricter regulations in Argentina, more and more Russians are choosing to travel to Brazil to give birth to children, who will obtain Brazilian nationality.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A war-fatigued and anxious Russia picks a new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97e61b3118214988415cf526ed9a32c0c9c889bc241f4929e9a55e6e33dadd93</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440--1588122e0cc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fuel shortages, drone strikes and mobilization rumors are fueling anxiety and war fatigue in Russia. As support for peace talks grows among Russians, the Kremlin is watching closely ahead of parliamentary elections.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Third malaria death linked to Frankfurt Airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0307a6a203b99b642bca985f6003b9fda9d9324c42008bde9fbbf4fbffcb5dc7</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-third-malaria-death-linked-to-frankfurt-airport/a-79315012--d744a8a0ae06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-third-malaria-death-linked-to-frankfurt-airport/a-79315012?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two new malaria cases have been registered this week near Frankfurt airport, two months after cases first emerged.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Ovechkin backs Putin party in campaign video</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a9806160ba5cd654339dc3e9014b7d0c454b5377341e699672d3e12fcd975d1</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772--a8049deceb76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey legend Alexander Ovechkin has lent Vladimir Putin's party a helping hand in its parliamentary election campaign. That's in keeping with a pattern of support by an athlete who claims not to be political.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia, Houthis exchange blows as conflict escalates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fc92bd501df3cc6465be5b3f84355408192aef932b126e224fac03369bb818e</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-houthis-exchange-blows-as-conflict-escalates/a-79313776--51d4bac0512e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-houthis-exchange-blows-as-conflict-escalates/a-79313776?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Five people were reportedly killed as the escalation between the two sides continues to spiral. The Houthis denied attacking Mecca, with Saudi Arabia saying one person was killed by drone shrapnel.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Judges: As AfD ascends, Germany must bolster justice system</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f97edb24969e706b50190737c0267c4eb1eef8d221db5ba19ced19864b3ae954</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/judges-as-afd-ascends-germany-must-bolster-justice-system/a-79314333--577c69414d59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/judges-as-afd-ascends-germany-must-bolster-justice-system/a-79314333?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German judges and prosecutors warn that the government needs to reform the laws covering state prosecutors to prevent "extremists in government" from abusing the legal system.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>As global crises grow, Germany cuts development aid</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a6a325e1cebfccd4b1e0ace5653f24c9e3107724220053e4b0070c20e1f4c12</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T14:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-global-crises-grow-germany-cuts-development-aid/a-79257532--7d61e729011c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-global-crises-grow-germany-cuts-development-aid/a-79257532?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The budget of Germany's Economic Cooperation and Development Ministry is set to shrink for the fifth consecutive year. Aid organizations warn that the cuts will have severe consequences for millions of people.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Smuggling suspected as more rare animals seen in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:001bd0d8c952a4776aaa282f9b18ad40160052c424566f39c121ea15034a77d0</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352--d0621e7dbde3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Orangutans, rare reptiles and other exotic animals are popping up in India, suggesting the country is becoming a major destination for trafficked wildlife.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: How disinformation fuels Houthi-Saudi conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c20417698600f2019aa371bf1dc2e3df0dde048b7829e31c4ca0a7b747fa2f76</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T12:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-how-disinformation-fuels-houthi-saudi-conflict/a-79307257--b5d0251bde9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-how-disinformation-fuels-houthi-saudi-conflict/a-79307257?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As fighting between the Houthis and Saudi Arabia escalates, old and repurposed videos have flooded social media, with many presented as fresh footage from the front lines.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa: Police find 9th body of woman amid spree fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d96c1c8eae994a9e118eaa857eea4ec42421ce30acb35ad65f845bfae8877164</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-police-find-9th-body-of-woman-amid-spree-fears/a-79310945--14212b985f47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-police-find-9th-body-of-woman-amid-spree-fears/a-79310945?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in South Africa have discovered the bodies of nine women east of Johannesburg in two months, stoking fears of a serial killer or group of killers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Europe seeks stricter age limits for TikTok, Instagram and Facebook</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fae31864d0231fa917bf096752bb612511a230a5eb6e7da7d1d728de2c2298ee</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T12:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/europe-seeks-stricter-age-limits-for-tiktok-instagram-and-facebook/a-79310207--9407f6c7e48f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/europe-seeks-stricter-age-limits-for-tiktok-instagram-and-facebook/a-79310207?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission wants to bar children under 13 from social media platforms and curb addictive features such as infinite scrolling. Companies that fail to comply could face hefty fines.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Germany's football team to 'reclaim the flag'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:015856b749276311dab198ab5340ac211db17a4873e5e1f13be82f710abd2748</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-germany-s-football-team-to-reclaim-the-flag/a-79307610--57ff88db5991.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-germany-s-football-team-to-reclaim-the-flag/a-79307610?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jürgen Klopp, Germany's new head coach, says he wants his team to reclaim pride in being German after recent political developments.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian President Vucic criticizes Kosovo war crimes verdict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:023b308b11d1f71db819192dc5ae372385079d8bf6edf34158e64a005655e77f</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-s-president-vucic-criticizes-kosovo-war-crimes-verdict/a-79307654--c1957e85b089.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbian-president-vucic-criticizes-kosovo-war-crimes-verdict/a-79307654?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The conviction of four former Kosovo Liberation Army leaders has drawn sharply different reactions across the Balkans. Serbia has accused the court of failing to fully address crimes against Serbs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>King Charles, Earl Spencer clash over Diana death once again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccce9a35703f76b470ee7af7237e2ae36554f93c4cf25af713b520dba5e2f404</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/king-charles-earl-spencer-clash-over-diana-death-once-again/a-79305876--fe22dce63256.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/king-charles-earl-spencer-clash-over-diana-death-once-again/a-79305876?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Buckingham Palace has rejected criticism of King Charles III in a new book by the brother of his late wife, Princess Diana. Earl Charles Spencer has been a fierce critic of his former brother-in-law for decades.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's Carney welcomes associate status idea in EU speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9d28c333a9d7b6315e206f7179b1e3b2984c3e4e0bf8d3161518b865a3fc8ce</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T10:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-s-carney-welcomes-associate-status-idea-in-eu-speech/a-79306191--f0a5083edd86.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-s-carney-welcomes-associate-status-idea-in-eu-speech/a-79306191?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mark Carney wants to strengthen Canada's ties to the European Union amid a growing rift with the US under Donald Trump. The US president has threatened to halt trade with Europe if it makes Canada an associate EU member.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jews once lived lived here: When houses tell stories</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:943854afe945bfee0d3a75aa587f9ab10114dbe5687c3cc2f2d4613ed7df2a71</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T09:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jews-once-lived-lived-here-when-houses-tell-stories/a-79264813--f29d1ad1c32d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jews-once-lived-lived-here-when-houses-tell-stories/a-79264813?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Time and again, residents tracing the history of their homes discover the lives of Jewish predecessors who fled or were deported amid stories of suffering and loss.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Fiji declares HIV a national crisis, 1 in 60 adults carry it</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e680715b515f05ed6cb832e146eca3e68cbf3b25736717bb6b2a1c5a558c567e</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T09:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fiji-declares-hiv-a-national-crisis-1-in-60-adults-carry-it/a-79300628--b877c6a68508.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fiji-declares-hiv-a-national-crisis-1-in-60-adults-carry-it/a-79300628?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fiji's government estimates that HIV prevalence has almost tripled in the last five years. It's expanding testing, prevention and treatment services. In 2025 the tiny island recorded 16 times more new cases than in 2019.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp's first Germany squad includes 44 players</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46daa53ba0b5394c335296bdbb2cb63ca31baad0cbc87d46825a9b66e3cc8439</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-s-first-germany-squad-includes-44-players/a-79289254--9874c23792d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-s-first-germany-squad-includes-44-players/a-79289254?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's new head coach Jürgen Klopp has named a huge squad for his first four games, splitting them into two groups. A host of new faces is included.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Australia to restrict student, backpacker visas in migration clampdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08690faca10e229fa893f43ff147122573fe04ebed92c35170e80865c92f617b</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-to-restrict-student-backpacker-visas-in-migration-clampdown/a-79302553--6c212210d6dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-to-restrict-student-backpacker-visas-in-migration-clampdown/a-79302553?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Australian interior minister said reducing migration was needed to address housing pressures. The changes come as the far right surges in the polls.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Mysterious explosions reported in Frankfurt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43511e47780588e034e6785b2d515678393b57aa2be13da8aaaf1acc0f337938</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-mysterious-explosions-reported-in-frankfurt/live-79300494--1397711c1e30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-mysterious-explosions-reported-in-frankfurt/live-79300494?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A cafe and kiosk were damaged overnight in Frankfurt, in what police said are the latest in a series of mysterious blasts in the area. Meanwhile, diesel prices in Germany have hit an all-time high. More on DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: New Delhi denies claims world leaders fell ill after BRICS summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83239cbd052c5e3aaf95166c56392b1fa380bb64408454d7374bf470838269fa</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-denies-claims-world-leaders-fell-ill-after-brics-summit/live-79300604--d5a9663f9e7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-denies-claims-world-leaders-fell-ill-after-brics-summit/live-79300604?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's Foreign Ministry rejected viral social media claims that leaders fell ill after the BRICS summit. Meanwhile, India defended its right to buy oil from diverse sources after the US passed a new sanctions bill.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
